7-4. Brief or Memorandum of Points and Authorities
(a) Content. In addition to complying with the applicable provisions of Civil L.R. 3-4, a 
brief or memorandum of points and authorities filed in support, opposition, or reply to a 
motion must contain:
(1) On the first page in the space opposite the caption and below the case number, 
the noticed hearing date and time; 
(2) If in excess of 10 pages, a table of contents and a table of authorities; 
(3) A statement of the issues to be decided;
(4) A succinct statement of the relevant facts; and

USDC Local Civil Rules – Effective May 1, 2026 CIV-61
(a) Petitions for instructions;
(b) Petitions for the payment of dividends to creditors;
(c) Petitions for confirmation of sales of property;
(d) Reports of the receiver;
(e) Motions for fees of the receiver or of any attorney, accountant or investigator, the 
notice to state the services performed and the fee requested; and
(f) Motions for discharge of the receiver.
